"text": "Share by Email (opens in a new tab)",
"href": "mailto:?subject=Facebook&body=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.facebook.com%2F1397566565864286+-+%E2%80%9CThe+most+Newtown+thing+I%E2%80%99ve+ever+seen+is+people+helping+other+Newtowners.%E2%80%9D++That+spirit+is+at+the+center+of+this+conversation.+New+episode+of+Two+Guys+and+a+Pint+drops+today.+%5Bopen.spotify.com%2Fepisode%2F7r8DYqRzUQLxfbc5iAEe4A%3Fsi%3DIvjmF1ucSvmtK9mhANlCYA&nd=1&dlsi=65f61...%5DMichelle+Embree+Ku+talked+about+property+taxes%2C+education+funding%2C+I-84%2C+affordable+housing%2C+local+volunteers%E2%80%94and+why+listening+at+the+more+than+the+1%2C000+doors+she%E2%80%99s+knocked+on+this+year%E2%80%94is+important.+Her+reason+is+simple%3A+%E2%80%9CI+want+to+know+what%E2%80%99s+on+your+mind+so+I+can+be+a+better+representative.%E2%80%9D++And%2C+don%E2%80%99t+miss+Michelle%E2%80%99s+answer+to+this+important+question%3A+What+would+be+your+signature+dish+if+you+opened+a+Newtown+restaurant%3F%E2%80%A6Two+Guys+And+A+Pint+#newtownct #podcast #cheesecake #volunteer #helpersMichelle Embree Ku Democrat for State Representative, 106th District"
},
{
"text": "Share by Email (opens in a new tab)",
"href": "mailto:?subject=Facebook&body=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.facebook.com%2F1397714169182859+-+The+Difference+is+Clear+Day+2%3A+Taxes+&+BudgetsFamilies+are+feeling+the+squeeze%E2%80%94and+the+difference+is+clear.In+2025%2C+Mitch+Bolinsky+voted+%2ANO+on+the+state+budget+that+included+a+%24250+increase+to+the+Earned+Income+Tax+Credit+for+eligible+working+families+with+children.+Michelle+Embree+Ku+supports+putting+money+back+in+families%E2%80%99+pockets+while+working+to+lower+energy+and+health+insurance+costs%E2%80%94the+everyday+costs+that+make+it+harder+to+make+ends+meet+and+drive+pressure+on+local+property+taxes.That%E2%80%99s+the+difference%21+Newtown+deserves+a+representative+who+puts+working+families+first.=#TheDifferenceIsClear #NewtownCT #CTPolitics #WorkingFamilies #CostOfLiving #CTEITC #lookitup*PA 25-168, §371 | HB 7287, House Roll Call Vote 290*  [www.cga.ct.gov/2025/VOTE/H/PDF/2025HV-00290-R00HB07287-HV.PDF]*The law added $250 to Connecticut’s EITC for qualifying taxpayers with at least one child, beginning with tax year 2025.* [cga.ct](www.cga.ct.gov/2025/rpt/pdf/2025-R-0093.pdf)Michelle Embree Ku Democrat for State Representative, 106th District"
},
